Article 20 Network platform service providers with a huge number of minor users or that have a significant impact on the group of minors shall perform the following obligations:
(1) During the design, research and development, operation and other stages of network platform services, fully consider the characteristics of minors' physical and mental health development, and regularly carry out impact assessments on the online protection of minors;
(2) Provide a minor mode or minor zone, etc., to facilitate minors' access to platform products or services beneficial to physical and mental health;
(3) Establish and improve the compliance system for the online protection of minors in accordance with state provisions, set up an independent institution mainly composed of external members, and supervise the situation of online protection of minors;
(4) Follow the principles of openness, fairness, and justice, formulate special platform rules, clarify the obligations of platform product or service providers regarding the online protection of minors, and prompt minor users in a conspicuous manner of the network protection rights they enjoy according to law and the remedies for network infringement;
(5) Cease providing services to platform product or service providers that violate laws or administrative regulations and seriously infringe upon the physical and mental health of minors or violate other legitimate rights and interests of minors;
(6) Publish a special social responsibility report on the online protection of minors every year, and accept social supervision.
The specific determination method for network platform service providers with a huge number of minor users or that have a significant impact on the group of minors as referred to in the preceding paragraph shall be separately formulated by the national cyberspace administration department together with the relevant departments.

Regulation on the Content of Network Information

Article 34 Where a minor or its guardian requests, according to law, to access, reproduce, correct, supplement, or delete the minor's personal information, the personal information processor shall comply with the following provisions:
(1) Provide convenient methods and channels to support the minor or its guardian in accessing the types and quantities of the minor's personal information, and shall not restrict the reasonable requests of the minor or its guardian;
(2) Provide convenient functions to support the minor or its guardian in reproducing, correcting, supplementing, or deleting the minor's personal information, and shall not impose unreasonable conditions;
(3) Promptly accept and process the application of the minor or its guardian for accessing, reproducing, correcting, supplementing, or deleting the minor's personal information; if the request of the minor or its guardian to exercise rights is refused, it shall inform the applicant in writing and state the reasons.
Where the minor or its guardian requests, according to law, to transfer the minor's personal information, if the conditions prescribed by the national cyberspace administration department are met, the personal information processor shall provide a means for the transfer.
